  "body": "The legacy service-marketplace booking and escrow-release routes inserted Payment rows and reported funds held or paid out without verified payment evidence. The user explicitly resolved SYS-C06: disable both writes. Both routed handlers now return HTTP 503 before reading Env or persistence, including for admins, invalid IDs and retries. Existing rows remain intact; no migration or provider activation is introduced.\n\nThe canonical contract records authority, state-preservation obligations, routing correspondence and trust limits. Historical nominal T3/T5 are marked superseded. Hspec executes the actual routed handlers with a poison Env (55 executions); source-contract negative controls detect restored effects and bypasses. No unrestricted Haskell or whole-system proof is claimed.\n\nProduction release and recovery inspect both Server.hs and API.hs from the exact candidate revision: constant rejection bodies, marketplace dispatch/order, and authenticated parent/root bindings must agree. This closes review finding 4059370277: retaining unused safe stubs while rerouting a financial endpoint is rejected. Identity ancestry and identical-migration protections remain required. Missing Git evidence is an error.\n\nA necessary release dependency also fixes the repeated hosted WebKit recovery-dialog dismissal failure by unmounting the closed dialog. The new regression detects the old behavior; browser assertions and timeouts are unchanged. The catalog decision explicitly classifies the verification binding constant.\n\nValidation at final source head `989d0663cc249bcee74331604561628d3435c961`: 89 related release/source-contract tests and catalog authority checks passed locally. Fresh PR CI and formal checks must pass before merge. Prior head `3e5563a2dd1c01d1c7b6f73ac3153681a9290a12` passed full CI 35563039207, formal 35563039148, social 35563039146, catalog 35563039163 and image build 35562811641. The final change affects host-side verification/release tooling and documentation; backend/API/UI sources match that built ancestor.\n\nStaging revision `7314245c17a1413df3d86ff5c0cf6dc78185ac78` passed exact-image health/version checks and six authenticated endpoint probes across unprivileged/admin roles, including duplicate releases; financial/booking/slot counts were unchanged. Tokens were removed and grants deactivated, retaining inert synthetic principal history. Final merged-artifact staging and production evidence remain required.\n\nUse the standard protected merge commit, preserving `3e5563a2dd1c01d1c7b6f73ac3153681a9290a12` as a distinct reviewed recovery ancestor. Its built image index is `sha256:ed842af824c2e1b9de08d608bf94c7f5364691f1903038652661f2055eb9e3fc`. Build the exact resulting main revision as the target. An initial squash without a compatible ancestor correctly remains blocked; the existing recovery ancestry rule is not weakened.\n\nReproduce: `node --test scripts/__tests__/legacy-escrow-contract.test.mjs`, `npm run test:production-release`, `npm run audit:catalog-lists`, and in tdf-hq `stack test --test-arguments='--match \"disabled legacy service marketplace financial writes\"'`. See formal/system/README.md for full solver/model/evidence commands and limitations. Follow-up to merged #455; independent approval and fresh checks are required. Production remains unchanged.\n\nReview comment 4059456754 references replay commit `9cceaffe`, not this PR's published head. Both local `git merge-base --is-ancestor 33083d469727da73e73ea4a2c2be5aaec130b137 989d0663cc249bcee74331604561628d3435c961` (exit 0) and GitHub compare confirm the fixture is an ancestor (ahead 16, behind 0; merge-base is 33083d469). The required standard merge preserves it in main even after branch deletion. Full-history CI checkouts retain the object. No squash/rebase integration is intended or authorized by this delivery plan.\n\nFinal verification checkpoint (2026-09-21T05:37:17.863313+00:00): all22 current-head checks succeeded, including CI35564368709, formal35564368761, social35564368738 and catalog35564368713. Local/hosted bounded model source digest matches:e832a562468f80d43c3a75738c3c7d0e52544a474b9551288f9e4a1192294715. Hosted merge candidate001ffeff and head989d066 share tree7d07d52d916906922e4f73f000aa8eb3e5c92073. Staging3e passed six actual503 assertions with unchanged financial/bookingcounts; expected immutable image observed. Read-only production preflight returnedready, with directMachine network probe failures and configured public fallback explicitly recorded. No independent approval is recorded; protected merge and exact merged-artifact backend production delivery remain pending.\n",
